WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.960
- [Narrator] Imagine a world
where the most powerful country

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:06.740
on earth in 2021 wasn't the United States,

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:07.944
but rather Spain.

00:00:07.944 --> 00:00:10.420
(dramatic suspenseful music)

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.240
And instead of setting up military bases

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.130
just in their own country,
they also set up bases

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.100
all around the world.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.390
Lots of those bases
are in former colonies,

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:22.120
but also there's a bunch
in the United States,

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.480
just imagine this.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.830
You zoom in to Fayetteville,
North Carolina,

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.360
and you see a huge military base.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:32.200
But it's not a US military
base, it's a Spanish base

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.393
on American soil, with lots of homes

00:00:34.393 --> 00:00:37.230
for the Spanish soldiers
and their families,

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.860
powerful weapons systems, aircraft,

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:42.010
all run by the Spanish military.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:43.520
Go inside of one of these bases

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.570
and it's all Spanish restaurants.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:48.190
Americans can't come in
here unless they work

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:49.570
for the Spanish government.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.670
And then imagine 100 more of these

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:54.200
all throughout the United
States on American soil,

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.303
and hundreds of more throughout the world.

00:00:56.303 --> 00:00:58.060
Or shift the scenario a little bit,

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.560
what if it was a country
that wasn't our ally,

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.870
a country like China?

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:04.870
What if they had military
bases not in the US,

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:06.913
but right up close to our border?

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:10.850
Powerful weapon systems
right off our shores

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:12.740
in islands in the Caribbean.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:15.440
If you're an American, you have to imagine

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:16.630
what that would feel like.

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:18.220
If you're not an American,

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.790
it's likely you already kind of know

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:22.090
what this feels like.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:24.455
The United States has an extensive network

00:01:24.455 --> 00:01:27.735
of military bases outside of our borders,

00:01:27.735 --> 00:01:30.210
hundreds of bases.

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.100
I've been fascinated for a very long time

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.930
about understanding these
US foreign bases abroad,

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:38.630
but I've never actually taken the time

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:41.620
to accurately map them, so let's do it.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:45.360
Let's map every single US
military base around the world.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.213
It turns out that's a huge task.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:50.870
- [Man] This is the story of the men

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:53.990
of the United States Army who
made this project possible,

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:57.016
and of man's never seizing
quest for knowledge.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:02:00.433
(offbeat dramatic music)

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.250
- [Man 2] This is a full armored division.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:05.950
To give you an idea of size,

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.750
each of those small dark squares

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.600
includes more than 1,000 men.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.680
- The United States military is bigger

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.290
than any of us can really fathom.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:17.210
It's so big that even the US military

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:20.550
doesn't know how big the US military is.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:24.200
Back in 2018, 1200 independent accountants

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.038
and analysts came in to try to audit

00:02:26.038 --> 00:02:28.380
the US Department of Defense,

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:32.450
basically try to get a paper
trail of how big this thing is,

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:34.360
how much money it spends, et cetera.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.280
And the Department of Defense
didn't pass the audit.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.740
They literally did not have the documents

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:42.200
or the knowledge to really piece together

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.410
a full scope of what this organization is,

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:47.140
how big it is, how much money it spends.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.990
So we don't know, nobody knows how big

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:51.740
the Pentagon is in all of its forms.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:54.060
All we do know is that objectively,

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:57.010
it is one of the, if not the largest

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:00.080
and most powerful
organization on the planet

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.040
and in the history of humanity.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.240
I mean if you have an organization

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:07.490
that's more powerful than
the Department of Defense

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:09.590
in the history of humans, let me know,

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:12.460
I want to know about it,
but as far as I can tell,

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.120
there's nothing bigger and more powerful

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:16.930
than the United States military in 2021.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:21.210
And much of the US military
is not actually in the US,

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:23.342
but it's actually outside of our borders,

00:03:23.342 --> 00:03:24.730
all around the world.

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:26.610
- [Man] This post is somewhere in Germany,

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:29.384
overlooking a sector of the Iron Curtain.

00:03:29.384 --> 00:03:31.620
- One of the first things that Joe Biden

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.540
and his administration did
when they came into power

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:35.320
a couple of weeks ago down the road

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.290
was ask for an assessment of,

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:40.580
how big is our military
presence around the whole world?

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:42.030
What is our strategy,

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:44.900
and what actually does
this presence look like?

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.560
- The Department will conduct
a global force posture review

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.600
of US military footprint,
resources, and strategies.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:52.670
- Footprint, I like that,
that's a nice thing,

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:55.054
what's our footprint,
how big is our footprint

00:03:55.054 --> 00:03:56.040
around the world?

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.920
We don't really know, the Pentagon

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.210
is gonna start to try to assess that.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.150
So, let's help the Pentagon out

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:05.790
and try to map every
single United States base

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:08.830
around the entire world.

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:09.686
Let's do it.

00:04:09.686 --> 00:04:13.103
(offbeat dramatic music)

00:04:20.395 --> 00:04:23.430
It wasn't too long ago when I used

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:25.930
to think that having military bases

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:29.070
in other countries was totally normal.

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:31.036
Doesn't every country have military bases

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:33.280
in other countries?

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:34.560
Yeah, anyway.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:36.450
This was sort of reinforced for me

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:37.560
when I was in college.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:40.510
I didn't internship at
NATO with the headquarters

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.110
of NATO, which was in Brussels.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:46.380
To get this job, I had to get
a secret security clearance

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:50.040
from the US government in order
to enter the military base,

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.500
which was NATO.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:52.500
This was really cool

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.350
because there was always
people comin' through NATO

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:56.183
that I got to meet.

00:04:56.183 --> 00:04:59.350
Like, my diplomacy hero Madeleine Albright

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:02.160
who used to be the Secretary
of State, or this guy.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:05.230
- It's a great honor
representing my country abroad

00:05:06.223 --> 00:05:08.370
for the last 37 years.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:09.310
- Good old Joe.

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:12.290
Hey Joe, I had no idea
you'd be President someday.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:13.220
Anyway, the big benefit

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:14.850
of having this secret security clearance

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:18.130
is that I could go into
any military base anywhere.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:19.821
And so on Saturdays, I would drive

00:05:19.821 --> 00:05:23.560
an hour from Brussels to a little village

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:26.680
in the Belgian countryside
where a military base

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:28.560
had been sort of plopped down

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.460
in the middle of the Belgian countryside

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:34.470
in between stone walls and quaint streets,

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:37.620
and sheep, and farming plots.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:39.700
Yeah, it's a little blurry in this map

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:42.160
because it's, you know, a military base

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:44.120
and sometimes they blur
the satellite imagery.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:45.620
Nothin' I can do about it, sorry.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.810
And as soon as I entered into the base,

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:49.550
went through all the security
and I was in the base,

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:51.800
I felt like I had left Belgium

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.870
and was suddenly entering
suburban American.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:56.560
- Welcome to the United States.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.110
- There was a Taco Bell and movie theaters

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:02.650
with American movies,
and all sorts of shops,

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:06.030
and yoga studios, and a grocery store

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:09.650
that had all of the products
that I was very used to,

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:11.940
all at the same prices I could get them

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:13.900
in the United States, even
though they had been flown

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:17.520
across the Atlantic and
brought to this place,

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.670
which is a very expensive thing to do.

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:22.495
It was a dream for me
as a poor college kid

00:06:22.495 --> 00:06:27.495
living in Brussels and
feeling a little bit homesick,

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:29.270
to be honest, and really figured out

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:30.380
culture shock at this point,

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.810
so yeah, I kind of loved it.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:34.430
And I was again, sort of,

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:36.370
doesn't everyone have military bases

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:38.100
in other countries and
they can sort of just go

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.950
to their military base, and it was just,

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:41.720
I was so naive.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:44.610
Mmm, alas, I've learned the truth.

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:48.277
(offbeat suspenseful music)

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:52.650
Luckily, I was able to talk to somebody

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:56.740
who literally wrote the book
on US military bases abroad.

00:06:56.740 --> 00:07:00.460
- Most US bases abroad look
like not-so-small US towns.

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:02.730
- Over the years, David
has been researching

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.340
and compiling a database

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:06.680
of all the US bases around the world.

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:09.210
The result is a very detailed audit

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:12.110
that hasn't really ever
been done to this degree.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:15.450
In fact, a few years ago, the
Pentagon's own research arm,

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:16.790
the RAND Corp,

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:20.767
was doing some research
on military bases abroad,

00:07:20.767 --> 00:07:23.160
and instead of using the Pentagon's list

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:24.991
of US military bases abroad,

00:07:24.991 --> 00:07:28.685
these guys used David's
list, like they used David,

00:07:28.685 --> 00:07:29.750
it was like he was a professor,

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:33.250
he's like an anthropologist,
he's not like a part of DoD.

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:35.580
And yet they're like,
this list that he made

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:39.770
is actually more authoritative
than the Pentagon's own list.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:41.690
- I mean I'm sort of honored,

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:46.646
but it's not a good sign if
the Pentagon research arm

00:07:46.646 --> 00:07:49.540
is using my list and not
the Pentagon's own list.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:51.360
- So I got a hold of David's list

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.070
and started wrestling with the data

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:55.300
and finding a way to display it on a map

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:57.380
so that I could get every single base

00:07:57.380 --> 00:07:58.600
to show somehow.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.020
After a few weeks of doing this,

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:03.933
I finally have a map, and
that map looks like this.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:14.065
Every dot on this map
is a US military base

00:08:14.065 --> 00:08:17.980
or installation of some
sort in a different country.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:19.430
Many of these dots are not placed

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:22.310
exactly where the base is,
because many of these bases

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.270
are clustered in areas.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:26.880
And if I try to map them
all in the exact spot

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.620
where they really are,
they would all just sort of

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:29.710
stack on top of each other,

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:31.210
and you wouldn't really
be able to see them.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:35.010
But these dots represent
every single base outside

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:37.730
of the United States from huge complexes

00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:41.470
the size of Rhode Island
to small air strips,

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:43.838
little facilities that
only house American drones

00:08:43.838 --> 00:08:47.070
or radar, or supplies.

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:50.830
This is all of them, and at
least all that we know of.

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:53.000
If you look at this map and you see

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.520
a base that you know of that is not here,

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:57.640
or one that is there that
doesn't belong there,

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.290
tell me about it, I want to know

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:03.020
because this is sort of hard
information to ascertain.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:05.130
The Pentagon is not very transparent,

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:07.510
and neither are host countries

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:09.309
about where certain bases are,

00:09:09.309 --> 00:09:11.210
and why they exist.

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:12.487
- Many of the bases around the world

00:09:12.487 --> 00:09:17.487
are, their existence
is due to an agreement

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:19.890
between the two countries

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:22.690
that is often not open to the public,

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:23.980
that is a secret.

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.660
Any errors here are mine and not David's.

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:30.880
All in all, the number here is about 750.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.698
750 US military bases big and small

00:09:33.698 --> 00:09:35.770
outside of the United States.

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:37.210
By outside of the United States,

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:41.100
I'm including US territories
that are not equal

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.190
to the United States.

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:45.720
Like Guam, Puerto Rico, et cetera.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:48.930
But in reality, we probably
don't know the real number

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:50.830
because that data just simply

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:53.010
is not transparently available to us.

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:54.896
There are a couple of major clusters here

00:09:54.896 --> 00:09:56.880
where the most bases exist.

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:00.180
One major one is Germany,
and the others are Japan

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:01.710
and South Korea.

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:04.507
These are basically
holdovers from World War II

00:10:04.507 --> 00:10:05.935
and the subsequent Korean War

00:10:05.935 --> 00:10:08.643
when the US, who won the war,

00:10:08.643 --> 00:10:11.660
came in and occupied these countries

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:14.120
in order to set up a new government,

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:17.210
write a new constitution, and
to help the post-war transfer

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:18.043
to the government.

00:10:18.043 --> 00:10:21.240
But, what's most interesting
to me aren't these clusters

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:22.930
that came about because of World War II,

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:27.240
but instead the far-flung,
sort of unexpected

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:28.640
or little-known places

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:32.040
that the US military
has a little footprint.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:33.745
All the dots in Africa,

00:10:33.745 --> 00:10:35.930
which have popped up in recent years,

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:38.677
as the US has expanded its presence there.

00:10:38.677 --> 00:10:41.380
These are usually small installations

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:43.240
that hold maybe a few soldiers,

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:47.034
or mainly private citizens who
are government contractors.

00:10:47.034 --> 00:10:49.470
And they mainly house things like drones,

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:51.575
or radar, or weapons systems.

00:10:51.575 --> 00:10:53.588
You also have this cluster of dots

00:10:53.588 --> 00:10:55.980
deep in the Indian Ocean,

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:58.710
which is the island of Diego Garcia,

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:00.112
which I've talked about at length

00:11:00.112 --> 00:11:03.702
of the US military's role
in displacing hundreds

00:11:03.702 --> 00:11:06.440
of local people to set up a base there.

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:09.200
Some of these dots are just air strips,

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:11.050
a runway in the middle of nowhere,

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:13.360
and these runways usually
belong to the host country,

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.859
and the US just rents
them for a period of time.

00:11:15.859 --> 00:11:19.070
Like this facility in the
middle of the desert in Oman.

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:22.380
Places like this exist to hold supplies

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:24.560
in case a war breaks.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:27.870
So the US maintains these
stockpiles of war supplies

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:30.108
all around the globe
so that they can strike

00:11:30.108 --> 00:11:31.680
at any point without having

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:33.978
to ramp up a war economy at home.

00:11:33.978 --> 00:11:37.628
It takes away a lot of the
friction from going to war.

00:11:37.628 --> 00:11:39.090
- It made it easier

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:41.730
for the US military to
launch offensive force,

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:46.147
the wars in Iraq and Afghanistan
were easier to launch

00:11:46.147 --> 00:11:50.190
because US has maintained a
huge infrastructure of bases.

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:51.842
- Some of these dots
don't represent a place

00:11:51.842 --> 00:11:55.409
where US soldiers are actually stationed,

00:11:55.409 --> 00:11:58.820
but instead it represents
where money from the Pentagon

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:02.276
has gone to influence or
build up infrastructure.

00:12:02.276 --> 00:12:05.273
For example, in Iceland,
the US is spending

00:12:05.273 --> 00:12:08.180
a lot of money, tens
of millions of dollars,

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:11.840
to upgrade this airport, the
airport that we all go through

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:13.260
when we're going to Iceland,

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:15.500
but doing it for military purposes

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:18.830
so that the US can use it,
can land there if needed.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:19.921
So next time you land in Iceland

00:12:19.921 --> 00:12:21.614
on your way to the Blue Lagoon,

00:12:21.614 --> 00:12:24.763
just know that you're passing
by one of these little dots.

00:12:26.074 --> 00:12:28.760
Over here in the Azores, these islands

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.740
that are owned by Portugal,

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:33.367
nearly 2,000 kilometers
away from any land mass,

00:12:33.367 --> 00:12:36.591
there is a group of US
military installations

00:12:36.591 --> 00:12:40.410
mainly used for refueling
and weapon storage.

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:41.550
And up here to Greenland,

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:44.890
and you'll see a little base way up high,

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:46.560
the most northern base in the world

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:48.730
where 140 Americans live.

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:49.835
Kinda looks interesting,

00:12:49.835 --> 00:12:51.380
would love to go there someday.

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:54.380
Way out here in the
Pacific, you've got loads

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:58.010
of remote military bases
owned by the United States.

00:12:58.010 --> 00:12:59.609
They're mainly small air strips,

00:12:59.609 --> 00:13:01.720
like this base on the southern tip

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:04.915
of this huge atoll of
the Marshall Islands.

00:13:04.915 --> 00:13:08.590
All right listen, I'm not gonna
explain every single base.

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:10.539
There are 750, maybe 800.

00:13:10.539 --> 00:13:12.980
There's a bunch of bases,
I just wanted to give you

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:15.100
a flavor of what some of these look like.

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:17.203
They're diverse, they're
all over the place,

00:13:17.203 --> 00:13:19.310
and they're fascinating to me.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:22.540
I have been compiling
accounts of people who live

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:23.754
next to US military bases.

00:13:23.754 --> 00:13:26.760
I have over 100 accounts from people

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:29.500
that, for Instagram, I want more.

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:33.320
I wanna make an entire video
about life next to a base.

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:36.110
And that is why I'm
calling it upon all of you.

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:38.790
